=== ANALYSIS (per token = totals / 33) ===
Thread-0 ledger: 92.2 ms/token vs measured 91.9 (10.88 tok/s) - balances to 0.3%.
  GEMV compute (MUL_MAT 29.3 + MUL_MAT_ID 28.4)   57.7 ms   PHYSICS (the weight reads)
  FLASH_ATTN compute                                1.8 ms
  ALL small-op compute combined                     1.6 ms
  BARRIERS, total                                  30.8 ms   33% of the token, ~19.4 us x ~1590 nodes
    of which after pure small ops                  20.2 ms   <- the prize
    after MUL_MAT/MUL_MAT_ID                       10.1 ms   (partly real imbalance)
The smoking gun: ADD runs 432 times/token, 0.35 ms of compute behind 7.7 ms of barriers (22x
overhead). The "serial small-op chain" from prereg #33 was never the ops - it is the sync around
them. Design implication: ggml_cpu_try_fuse_ops already exists and the maintainers' own TODO says
fusion should move to planning time - extending fusion coverage over elementwise chains removes
the node boundary AND its barrier in one accepted-shape change. Even half of the 20.2 ms is
+12-15% decode; the staked +18-35% band holds.
